  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Phenol has activating (electron releasing) $-\\mathrm{OH}$ group and bromine water supplies $\\mathrm{Br}^{+}$ ion easily, hence under such conditions reaction does not stop at monobromo or dibromo stage but a fully brominated $(2,4,6$,-tribromophenol) compound is the final product.\n<img src=\"assets\\st0175_fada104c198e.png\"><br>"
  }
